<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan central bank sets Sunday weekly holiday.</title>
<headline>Pakistan central bank sets Sunday weekly holiday.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The State (central) Bank of Pakistan (SBP) said on Tuesday it would revert to Sunday as the weekly day off instead of Friday, starting March 2, to comply with the switch ordered by new Prime Minister Nawaz Sharif.</p>
<p>An SBP circuler said the bank would observe Friday as a half working day, closing offices at 0730 GMT, while on other week days it will remain open until 1200 GMT.</p>
<p>Bankers said all banks and financial institutions in Pakistan would follow the SBP office timings and observe Sunday as the weekly holiday.</p>
</text>
